A named remote profile whose saved library contains only its active model still lists the other models advertised by that active provider, and both dashboard requests retain the profile query parameter."},{"markdown":"An explicitly selected Remote Legacy transport can read its gateway's default model catalog through authenticated HTTP without enabling Dashboard-only model-library mutations.","startLine":35,"endLine":35,"text":"An explicitly selected Remote Legacy transport can read its gateway's default model catalog through authenticated HTTP without enabling Dashboard-only model-library mutations."},{"markdown":"The actual raw Agent server exposes authenticated `GET /api/model/options` and can omit `/api/model/library`. [[src/main/remote-models.ts#remoteListModels]] keeps its existing library-to-options fallback, and the registered `list-models` callback admits this read for the default/server profile. The preload call carries no explicit profile argument; this repair does not add named raw-server routing.","startLine":37,"endLine":37,"text":"The actual raw Agent server exposes authenticated GET /api/model/options and can omit /api/model/library. src/main/remote-models.ts#remoteListModels keeps its existing library-to-options fallback, and the registered list-models callback admits this read for the default/server profile. The preload call carries no explicit profile argument; this repair does not add named raw-server routing."},{"markdown":"An explicitly selected named Remote Legacy profile is refused before HTTP dispatch rather than silently reading the gateway's default or process-profile catalog.","startLine":41,"endLine":41,"text":"An explicitly selected named Remote Legacy profile is refused before HTTP dispatch rather than silently reading the gateway's default or process-profile catalog."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/remote-profile-selection.ts#getRemoteSelectedProfile]] resolves the selected profile for the captured active connection. Named Dashboard requests